    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The village sits along Illinois Route 127, which hugs the east edge of its center.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Butler%2C_Illinois",
      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "poor",
      "qualityReason": "route_only"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "From Butler, IL 127 leads southeast 4 miles to Hillsboro, the county seat, and north‑northwest 8 miles to Raymond.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Butler%2C_Illinois",
      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "poor",
      "qualityReason": "route_only"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Waterway-wise, Butler drains east to Cress Creek, a south‑flowing tributary of the Middle Fork of Shoal Creek, and west to Brush Creek, a tributary of the West Fork of Shoal Creek.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Butler%2C_Illinois",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "poor",
      "qualityReason": "vague"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Shoal Creek, fed by those tributaries, eventually joins the Kaskaskia River.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8
      ],
